[[:db/cas 17592186089187 :answer/value "$4.8$ tons and $3.2$ tons" "$3.2$ tons and $4.8$ tons"] [:db/cas 17592186089183 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186089187] [:db/cas 17592186092502 :question/worked-solution nil "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part} = \\textrm{percentage} \\times \\textrm{total}\n$$\n\nLet $x$ be the number of tons of $55\\%$ carbon steel. Since the mixture must total $8$ tons, there will be $8-x$ tons of $30\\%$ carbon steel.\n\nWe organize this information in a percentage–total–part table:\n\n| % Carbon | Total (tons) | Part Carbon (tons) |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $55$ | $x$ | $0.55x$ |\n| $30$ | $8-x$ | $0.30(8-x)$ |\n| $40$ | $8$ | $0.40\\cdot 8$ |\n\nThe parts carbon in the two starting amounts add up to the part carbon in the final mixture. Therefore,\n\n$$\n0.55x + 0.30(8-x) = 0.40\\cdot 8\n$$\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.55x + 2.4 - 0.30x &= 3.2 \\\\\n0.25x + 2.4 &= 3.2 \\\\\n0.25x &= 0.8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $100$ allows us to solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25x &= 80 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{80}{25} \\\\\nx &= 3.2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe amount of $30\\%$ carbon steel is $8-3.2=4.8$ tons.\n\nTherefore, mix **$3.2$ tons of $55\\%$ carbon steel and $4.8$ tons of $30\\%$ carbon steel**, in the order asked."] [:db/ensure 17592186089187 :answer/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186089183 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186092502 :question/validate]]
